@host = http://localhost:4004

### 1. Read customers (should return 2 records)
GET {{host}}/master-data/Customers

### 2. Create a valid contact (should return 201)
POST {{host}}/master-data/CustomerContacts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer_ID": "c1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
  "firstName": "Neha",
  "lastName": "Rao",
  "email": "neha@acme.com",
  "phone": "+919800000003"
}

### 3. Invalid email (should return 400)
POST {{host}}/master-data/CustomerContacts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer_ID": "c1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
  "firstName": "Test",
  "email": "not-an-email"
}

### 4. Contact with no email and no phone (should return 400)
POST {{host}}/master-data/CustomerContacts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer_ID": "c1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
  "firstName": "Test"
}

### 5. Duplicate category code (should return 409)
POST {{host}}/master-data/IssueCategories
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "NETWORK",
  "name": "Duplicate"
}

### 6. SLA policy where resolution is shorter than first response (should return 400)
POST {{host}}/master-data/SLAPolicies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Bad policy",
  "priority": "P1",
  "customerTier": "Silver",
  "firstResponseMins": 60,
  "resolutionMins": 30
}

### 7. Negative product price (should return 400)
POST {{host}}/master-data/Products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productCode": "PRD-999",
  "name": "Bad product",
  "productType": "PHYSICAL",
  "billingModel": "ONE_TIME",
  "unitPrice": -10
}

### 8. Delete a customer (should return 405)
DELETE {{host}}/master-data/Customers(c1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001)